                    "label": "Stage",
                    "type": "pill",
                    "width": "130px"
                },
                {
                    "align": "right",
                    "field": "premium",
                    "label": "Premium",
                    "type": "number",
                    "width": "120px"
                }
            ]
        },
        "description": "Column config array: [{ field, label?, type, width?, align?, refTable? }]. type ∈ text | reference | pill | number | date | boolean | icon. DATE COLUMNS always render in the timezone and date format of the CURRENT USER: by default (`dateDisplay: \"auto\"`) the value the platform already localized is used, and an optional per-column `dateDisplay` ∈ auto | datetime | date | time | relative formats the raw UTC value against the user profile instead (e.g. `\"dateDisplay\":\"relative\"` → \"2 hours ago\", `\"date\"` → date only). Pill columns auto-color each distinct value (stable). Optional per-column override `pillColors`: an object map of rule → color, e.g. { \"Referral\": \"critical\", \">100\": \"positive\", \"10..20\": \"warning\", \"Bound\": \"#0a7\" }. Rules support exact string match and numeric comparisons (>, <, >=, <=, =) + ranges (min..max); color is a tone (info/warning/critical/positive/neutral/purple/teal/pink) or a hex. First match wins; unmatched values fall back to the auto color. INLINE EDIT: add `editable:true` to a column; `editor` ∈ text (default) | choice. For choice, supply `choices` ([\"Open\",\"Closed\"] or [{label,value}]) — OR leave `choices` empty and, when bound to a real Table, the component auto-loads that field choices from the dictionary (sys_choice). An editable choice shows as a pill/text when idle and a dropdown when clicked. Saving is controlled by Edit save mode; PATCH targets the list table + the row sys_id. ROLE-GATING: add `roles` (array or CSV, e.g. [\"admin\",\"x_scope.role3\"]) to a column to show it only to users with one of those roles — requires the Role-based columns property ON.",
        "fieldType": "json",
        "label": "Columns",
        "name": "columns",
        "valueType": "string"
    },
    {
        "defaultValue": {
            "items": []
        },
        "description": "EXTRA columns the USER can add from the Columns picker, but which are NOT shown until they do — the \"available\" half of the OOB Edit-columns experience. Same item shape as Columns. Use it when the list should open on a tight default set (say 4 columns) while letting people reveal the other 5 when they need them. Their fields are fetched with every page, so switching one on is instant and never re-queries. A field listed in BOTH properties stays visible by default (Columns wins).",
        "fieldType": "json",
        "label": "Available columns (optional)",
        "name": "availableColumns",
        "valueType": "string"
    },
    {
        "defaultValue": 20,
        "description": "Rows per page (ungrouped) or top-level groups per page (grouped).",
        "fieldType": "number",
        "label": "Page size",
        "name": "pageSize",
        "valueType": "string"
    },
    {
        "defaultValue": "10,20,50,100",
        "description": "Comma-separated page-size options.",
        "fieldType": "string",
        "label": "Page sizes",
        "name": "pageSizes",
        "valueType": "string"
    },
    {
        "defaultValue": true,
        "description": "Show the \"Records per page\" selector in the footer. Always visible when on — even on a single page — matching the OOB list.",
        "fieldType": "boolean",
        "label": "Show page-size control",
        "name": "showPageSizeControl",
        "valueType": "string"
    },
    {
        "defaultValue": true,
        "description": "Click a column header to sort (server-side re-fetch).",
        "fieldType": "boolean",
        "label": "Enable sort",
        "name": "enableSort",
        "valueType": "string"
    },
    {
        "defaultValue": true,
        "description": "Drag the right edge of a header to resize a column.",
        "fieldType": "boolean",
        "label": "Enable column resize",
        "name": "enableResize",
        "valueType": "string"
    },
    {
        "defaultValue": true,
        "description": "Let users drag a column header onto another to reorder columns (disabled while grouped).",
        "fieldType": "boolean",
        "label": "Enable column reorder",
        "name": "enableColumnReorder",
        "valueType": "string"
    },
    {
        "defaultValue": true,
        "description": "Show the cog button that opens the \"Personalize List Columns\" dialog — a two-pane Available/Selected transfer where each user picks which columns they see, in which order, plus the display options below. Turn off to lock the list to exactly the columns you configured.",
        "fieldType": "boolean",
        "label": "Enable column personalization",
        "name": "enableColumnPersonalization",
        "valueType": "string"
    },
    {
        "defaultValue": "none",
        "description": "Row selection mode.",
        "fieldType": "choice",
        "label": "Selection mode",
        "name": "selectionMode",
        "typeMetadata": {
            "choices": [
                {
                    "label": "None",
                    "value": "none"
                },
                {
                    "label": "Single",
                    "value": "single"
                },
                {
                    "label": "Multi",
                    "value": "multi"
                }
            ],
            "schema": {
                "enum": [
                    "none",
                    "single",
                    "multi"
                ],
                "type": "string"
            }
        },
        "valueType": "string"
    },
    {
        "defaultValue": false,
        "description": "Fire Row clicked when a non-control area of a row is clicked.",
        "fieldType": "boolean",
        "label": "Enable row click",
        "name": "enableRowClick",
        "valueType": "string"
    },
    {
        "defaultValue": "auto",
        "description": "For editable columns: auto = save on blur / dropdown change; manual = show a Save ✓ (and Cancel) icon that commits.",
        "fieldType": "choice",
        "label": "Edit save mode",
        "name": "editSaveMode",
        "typeMetadata": {
            "choices": [
                {
                    "label": "Auto save",
                    "value": "auto"
                },
                {
                    "label": "Manual save (icon)",
